menu "IDPS marker"

    config MARKER_IR_GPIO
        int "IR LED GPIO"
        default 1
        help
            The GPIO driving the IR LED (through a 100 ohm resistor for a 5 mm LED, or a MOSFET
            for a high-power one). On the Seeed XIAO ESP32-C5, GPIO1 is pin D0 (check Seeed's
            pinout for your board).

    config MARKER_PREVIEW_GPIO
        int "Preview LED GPIO (-1: none)"
        default 27
        help
            A visible LED that shows the same code (HIGH on, LOW off), to see the marker working
            without an IR camera. The XIAO ESP32-C5's user LED is GPIO27.

    config MARKER_PREVIEW_ACTIVE_LOW
        bool "Preview LED lights when its pin is low"
        default y

    config MARKER_DEFAULT_ID
        int "Marker ID at first start (0-255; change later with the 'id' command)"
        range 0 255
        default 1

    config MARKER_PWM_HZ
        int "PWM frequency (Hz)"
        default 200000
        help
            The HIGH and LOW levels are PWM duty cycles. It must be much faster than the camera
            exposure (0.5 ms), so each exposure averages many cycles: 200 kHz gives 100.

endmenu
